# Registers docs/decisions/0005-batched-deletion.md as a proposed Decision
# vertex. Design-only: implementation remains a separately authorized,
# firewalled kernel batch under invariant-kernel-extension.
"@context": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/context/v1"
"@id": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/decision-0005-batched-deletion"
"@type": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/ontology/Decision"
label: "ADR 0005: unconditional S3 multi-object deletion"
timestamp: "2026-08-23T18:32:39Z"
source: "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/path/docs/decisions/0005-batched-deletion.md"
requires: "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/decision-0001-atomic-keyspace"
references:
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-kernel-extension"
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-13-state"
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-08-dependency-boundary"
statement: >
  PROPOSED, design-only; no implementation or publication is authorized.
  Adds AtomicKeyspace::delete_objects beside the published, frozen
  delete_many contract: sequential S3 DeleteObjects transport chunks of at
  most 1,000 unique keys, with one ordered Ok(deleted) or typed failure per
  admitted key. Valid mixed Deleted/Error responses are ordinary partial
  success; a request-level or invalid-response ambiguity marks the current
  chunk Unconfirmed and the untouched tail NotAttempted, so replay is
  idempotent and no success is fabricated. Hard boundaries: batch is
  transport, never a cross-key transaction; batched conditional delete is
  permanently absent and delete_if_match remains per-key; the raw primitive
  writes no tombstone, bumps no incarnation counter, and touches no trim
  certificate, maintenance fence, or v3 chunk. The named consumer is
  wholesale deletion of immutable, write-refused repository epochs, without
  coupling the kernel to epoch types or treating LIST as inventory authority.
  Proof plan A36-A45 covers admission, 1,000-key boundaries, deterministic
  partial-batch and whole-response loopback cuts, resumability, lifecycle
  non-effects, unconditional/non-atomic behavior, unsupported backends, and
  coexistence with unchanged delete_many/delete_if_match. Publication, if
  accepted and implemented in one later kernel batch, targets the next free
  0.4.x release and requires ci-dev plus real-S3 witnesses.
